# Copy to .dev.vars for local development (gitignored).
# Production secrets are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>` — never in wrangler.toml.
# Cloudflare account credentials are CI-ONLY (GitHub Actions secrets) — never on a laptop.

# --- Secrets used by the site Worker ---

# Cloudflare Turnstile (S2.2+). The deployed sitekey lives in wrangler.toml;
# the real secret is a Worker/repo secret. To exercise forms locally, use the
# official always-pass TEST PAIR together (mixing real+test never verifies):
# PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# --- Optional local overrides ---

# Launch mode override (defaults to "prelaunch"):
# LAUNCH_MODE=prelaunch

# --- Licence issuance (S12.4). Production: `wrangler secret put <NAME>` ---
#
# ⛔ SIGNING_KEY_JWK IS THE PRIVATE SIGNING KEY AND THE WHOLE COMMERCIAL MODEL. A leak is unlimited
# (it authorises MINTING, not one licence), unrevocable (verification is offline) and UNDETECTABLE
# (deployments never call home). Generate it with the CEREMONY in README.md — never on a shared machine,
# never into a file, never into a password manager.
#
# SIGNING_KEY_JWK={"kty":"OKP",...}     # PRIVATE JWK — production only, never a real value in a repo
# SIGNING_PUBLIC_JWK={"kty":"OKP",...}  # public half; used to self-verify a key before it is sent
# SIGNING_KID=k2026                     # which key in the SET minted it (D4). Never reused.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=...                       # guards /api/admin/*. A FLOOR — Cloudflare Access is the real control.
